{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ovtjqyyakovslz7kklos7woee3ifztg24yoyxiskbrh3tgx3poua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01RuBw2QDBUu9ErF2UXbgpWf","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"fileKey":"qYmJPYhan4qnoskPJ57RhI","description":"Read all text from Start Here and Foundations pages","code":"const out=[];\nfor (const id of ['0:1','1:2']) {\n  const p = figma.root.children.find(n=>n.id===id);\n  await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(p);\n  out.push('=== '+p.name);\n  const walk=(n,d)=>{ let s='  '.repeat(d)+n.type+' '+n.id+' \"'+n.name+'\" '+Math.round(n.width||0)+'x'+Math.round(n.height||0);\n    if(n.type==='TEXT') s+=' :: '+n.characters.replace(/\\n/g,' | ');\n    if(n.fills&&n.fills.length&&n.fills[0].type==='SOLID'&&n.type!=='TEXT'){const c=n.fills[0].color;s+=' fill#'+[c.r,c.g,c.b].map(v=>Math.round(v*255).toString(16).padStart(2,'0')).join('');}\n    out.push(s); if(n.children&&d<6) n.children.forEach(c=>walk(c,d+1));};\n  p.children.forEach(c=>walk(c,0));\n}\nreturn out.join('\\n');"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":7926,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":970,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14ea5b3b-ffb1-472a-8af8-83f665335b49","uuid":"4b8b9b2a-40c3-4edc-9a31-1354d533f89d","timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:45:53.374Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01RuBw2QDBUu9ErF2UXbgpWf","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01RuBw2QDBUu9ErF2UXbgpWf","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== 00 · Start Here 设计任务\nFRAME 2:2 \"Start Here · Brief\" 1440x5775 fill#ffffff\n  FRAME 2:3 \"Header\" 1440x321 fill#612a74\n    TEXT 2:4 \"LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\" 1312x21 :: LEVEL L2 · DESIGN TASK · v2\n    TEXT 2:5 \"Chat Bot AI — AI assistant app\" 1312x60 :: Chat Bot AI — AI assistant app\n    TEXT 2:6 \"Design the complete Chat Bot AI mobile app: Sam Rivera logs in, browses past chats, generated images and PDF exports, starts a new chat, continues a conversation that ends with a generated image, exports it as PDF, and manages profile, theme and cloud storage. Canvas 428 × 928, light mode only. Home, the conversation and Cloud Space may scroll vertically. Today is Dec 30, 2023. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\" 1312x104 :: Design the complete Chat Bot AI mobile app: Sam Rivera logs in, browses past chats, generated images and PDF exports, starts a new chat, continues a conversation that ends with a generated image, exports it as PDF, and manages profile, theme and cloud storage. | Canvas 428 × 928, light mode only. Home, the conversation and Cloud Space may scroll vertically. Today is Dec 30, 2023. Work in your own new Figma file — this file is read-only reference.\n  FRAME 2:7 \"Body\" 1440x5454\n    FRAME 2:8 \"How to work\" 1312x289\n      TEXT 2:9 \"How to work\" 1312x33 :: How to work\n      TEXT 2:10 \"1. Build exactly the 12 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in screen order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. 3. The brand primary color and the typefaces in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself (neutrals, text, surfaces, success / warning / error / disabled, storage-breakdown colors), plus type scale, spacing, radii and elevation, and apply them consistently. 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button, a default Text Field and the platform shell (status bar, home indicator). Design all other states, the headers, sheets, dialogs, message bubbles and every business component as reusable components in your file. 5. Use the logo, generated images, PDF icon and icons from 04 · Media. People have no photos: use Avatar_Neutral or initials. 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. Long answers may be cut off where the frame ends; everything listed must still be visible. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\" 1312x240 :: 1. Build exactly the 12 frames below, named exactly as listed (one state per frame), and wire them as a clickable prototype with the listed links. | 2. Everything in “Must include” must appear on that frame. The lists are grouped by subject and sorted alphabetically — they are not in screen order and say nothing about layout, grouping, emphasis or styling. Those are your decisions. | 3. The brand primary color and the typefaces in 01 · Foundations are fixed. Define every other color yourself (neutrals, text, surfaces, success / warning / error / disabled, storage-breakdown colors), plus type scale, spacing, radii and elevation, and apply them consistently. | 4. 02 · Components gives only a default Button, a default Text Field and the platform shell (status bar, home indicator). Design all other states, the headers, sheets, dialogs, message bubbles and every business component as reusable components in your file. | 5. Use the logo, generated images, PDF icon and icons from 04 · Media. People have no photos: use Avatar_Neutral or initials. | 6. Copy and data must match “Fixed data” exactly. Long answers may be cut off where the frame ends; everything listed must still be visible. This brief wins over anything you may know of the original kit.\n    FRAME 2:11 \"Frames · goals · must include · links\" 1312x2476\n      TEXT 2:12 \"Frames · goals · must include · links\" 1312x33 :: Frames · goals · must include · links\n      TEXT 2:13 \"Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\" 1312x23 :: Frame names are fixed. Must-include lists are grouped by subject and sorted A–Z: they state what is on the screen, never where it goes or how it looks.\n      FRAME 2:14 \"Frame cards\" 1312x2388\n        FRAME 2:15 \"01_Login\" 632x350 fill#f7f7fa\n          TEXT 2:16 \"01_Login\" 582x27 :: 01_Login\n          TEXT 2:17 \"Goal: Sign in to the account.\" 582x21 :: Goal: Sign in to the account.\n          TEXT 2:18 \"MUST INCLUDE\" 582x17 :: MUST INCLUDE\n          TEXT 2:19 \"• Actions: Forgot Password? · Login · “Don’t have an account?” Sign Up • Brand: logo • Copy: “Login to your account” • Form: Email “sam.rivera@example.com” · Password entered (masked, can be shown or hidden) • Legal: Terms of use · Privacy policy • Social sign-in: “Or login with” · Facebook · Google\" 582x147 :: • Actions: Forgot Password? · Login · “Don’t have an account?” Sign Up | • Brand: logo | • Copy: “Login to your account” | • Form: Email “sam.rivera@example.com” · Password entered (masked, can be shown or hidden) | • Legal: Terms of use · Privacy policy | • Social sign-in: “Or login with” · Facebook · Google\n          TEXT 2:20 \"LINKS\" 582x17 :: LINKS\n          TEXT 2:21 \"→ Login → 02_Home_Chats\" 582x21 :: → Login → 02_Home_Chats\n        FRAME 2:22 \"02_Home_Chats\" 632x413 fill#f7f7fa\n          TEXT 2:23 \"02_Home_Chats\" 582x27 :: 02_Home_Chats\n          TEXT 2:24 \"Goal: Find a past conversation or start a new one.\" 582x21 :: Goal: Find a past conversation or start a new one.\n          TEXT 2:25 \"MUST INCLUDE\" 582x17 :: MUST INCLUDE\n          TEXT 2:26 \