utral avatar • Default Button, default Text Field, platform shell\" 596x161 :: • Frame list and exact names | • Must-include content per frame (what, not how) | • Navigation structure and links | • All data and copy | • Brand primary color + Bricolage Grotesque and Nunito | • Media: logo, generated images, PDF icon, icons, neutral avatar | • Default Button, default Text Field, platform shell\n        FRAME 2:136 \"Yours (designer decides)\" 644x243 fill#f7f7fa\n          TEXT 2:137 \"Yours (designer decides)\" 596x24 :: Yours (designer decides)\n          TEXT 2:138 \"• Layout, grouping, order and emphasis on every screen • All other colors: neutrals, text, surfaces, semantic and storage-breakdown colors • Type scale, spacing, radii, elevation • All states: selected view and theme, pressed, disabled, focused, destructive • Headers, message bubbles, chat list items, sheets, dialogs and all business components • How storage usage is visualised\" 596x161 :: • Layout, grouping, order and emphasis on every screen | • All other colors: neutrals, text, surfaces, semantic and storage-breakdown colors | • Type scale, spacing, radii, elevation | • All states: selected view and theme, pressed, disabled, focused, destructive | • Headers, message bubbles, chat list items, sheets, dialogs and all business components | • How storage usage is visualised\n    FRAME 2:139 \"How it is evaluated\" 1312x296\n      TEXT 2:140 \"How it is evaluated\" 1312x33 :: How it is evaluated\n      TEXT 2:141 \"Your file is compared with the brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any reference.\" 1312x23 :: Your file is compared with the brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any reference.\n      TEXT 2:142 \"1. Checklist coverage per frame 2. Data & copy accuracy 3. Flow & prototype completeness 4. Information hierarchy 5. Visual quality & consistency of your own system 6. Component reuse 7. State design (current view and theme, sender of each message, sheets and dialogs over their parent, destructive actions)\" 1312x168 :: 1. Checklist coverage per frame | 2. Data & copy accuracy | 3. Flow & prototype completeness | 4. Information hierarchy | 5. Visual quality & consistency of your own system | 6. Component reuse | 7. State design (current view and theme, sender of each message, sheets and dialogs over their parent, destructive actions)\n      TEXT 2:143 \"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 12 named frames, your components and the prototype.\" 1312x24 :: Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 12 named frames, your components and the prototype.\n=== 01 · Foundations 视觉规范\nFRAME 3:2 \"Foundations\" 1200x2048 fill#ffffff\n  TEXT 3:3 \"Foundations · Chat Bot AI\" 1072x48 :: Foundations · Chat Bot AI\n  TEXT 3:4 \"Fixed: the brand primary color and the two typefaces below — they carry the Chat Bot AI identity. Everything else is yours to define and apply consistently: neutrals and grays, text colors, surfaces and backgrounds, semantic colors (success, warning, error, disabled), storage-breakdown colors, type scale, weights per role, spacing, radii and elevation.\" 1072x72 :: Fixed: the brand primary color and the two typefaces below — they carry the Chat Bot AI identity. Everything else is yours to define and apply consistently: neutrals and grays, text colors, surfaces and backgrounds, semantic colors (success, warning, error, disabled), storage-breakdown colors, type scale, weights per role, spacing, radii and elevation.\n  FRAME 3:5 \"Brand color\" 1072x314\n    TEXT 3:6 \"Brand color\" 1072x30 :: Brand color\n    FRAME 3:7 \"Brand primary\" 240x272\n      RECTANGLE 3:8 \"Rectangle\" 240x140 fill#612a74\n      TEXT 3:9 \"Brand primary\" 240x24 :: Brand primary\n      TEXT 3:10 \"#612A74\" 240x21 :: #612A74\n      TEXT 3:11 \"The Chat Bot AI brand color. Where and how much to use it is your decision.\" 240x63 :: The Chat Bot AI brand color. Where and how much to use i